      "description": "Scan locally for nearby smart-glasses Bluetooth signals and get a clear alert when a likely device is close.\n\nAntiZuck uses your device to show active signals that may come from smart glasses, including Ray-Ban Meta, Snap Spectacles, Amazon Echo Frames, and RayNeo. It also shows repeat sightings, confidence, and rough proximity.\n\nFEATURES\n\n• Live signal field: likely glasses appear as blips with rough proximity and confidence\n• Local alerts when a likely device starts broadcasting — even when the app is closed, when iOS permits background scanning\n• Sightings history: repeat encounters, confidence, distance, and why each signal was flagged\n• Add familiar glasses to Your Circle with custom labels, optional relationships, and per-device alert controls\n• Show rough proximity in feet or meters\n• Snooze alerts for an hour or the evening, right from the notification\n• Home Screen and Lock Screen widgets with the latest status and a pause button\n• Control Center toggle to pause or resume scanning, assignable to the Action Button\n• No account, no ads, completely local and private\n\nPrivacy stays local. The app does not identify people, record audio or video, track location, or upload signal history. Detection is best-effort and depends on what nearby devices advertise over Bluetooth. Smart glasses mostly broadcast at power-on, pairing, and case-open, so coverage is opportunistic.",
